concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Section 10"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Section 49J of the Principal Act is amended by omitting paragraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph: \"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the Registrar of the court of any person, including: (i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in this paragraph called the 'owner'); or (ii) the defendant; about the affairs (including the nature and location of any property) of: (iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or both; and (iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the defendant, or both—that person; and\". (2) An ancillary ordenriay be made under paragraph 49J (1) (c), as amended by this Act, in relation to restraining orders whether made before or after the commencement of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Section 49J of the Principal Act is amended by omitting paragraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph: \"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the Registrar of the court of any person, including: (i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in this paragraph called the 'owner'); or (ii) the defendant; about the affairs (including the nature and location of any property) of: (iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or both; and (iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the defendant, or both—that person; and\". (2) An ancillary ordenriay be made under paragraph 49J (1) (c), as amended by this Act, in relation to restraining orders whether made before or after the commencement of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dab2c2c4bee89c47ab93a927eec11d863dd166e432be8f5fe65562fbfcc6a3d3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-10-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-10-ss-2 ;
