concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-49 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49 Section 49"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-49 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Section 57 of the Principal Act is amended: (a) by inserting in subparagraph (2) (e) (i) \"that is a pecuniary penalty order\" after \"confiscation order\"; (b) by omitting from subparagraph (2) (e) (ii) \"confiscation order\" and substituting \"pecuniary penalty order\"; (c) by omitting from paragraph (2) (e) \"when the confiscation order is satisfied or otherwise ceases to be in force\" and substituting \", upon the pecuniary penalty order being satisfied or otherwise ceasing to be in force, to the extent that the property to which the restraining order relates is the same as the property that is sold or otherwise disposed of to satisfy the pecuniary penalty order and pay the costs, charges, expenses and remuneration referred to in subsection 49 (6)\"; (d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (g) \"19 or\" after \"section\". (2) The amendments made by subsection (1) apply in relation to restraining orders made before or after the commencement of this section.  Crimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2) No. 123, 1991 Production orders" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Section 57 of the Principal Act is amended: (a) by inserting in subparagraph (2) (e) (i) \"that is a pecuniary penalty order\" after \"confiscation order\"; (b) by omitting from subparagraph (2) (e) (ii) \"confiscation order\" and substituting \"pecuniary penalty order\"; (c) by omitting from paragraph (2) (e) \"when the confiscation order is satisfied or otherwise ceases to be in force\" and substituting \", upon the pecuniary penalty order being satisfied or otherwise ceasing to be in force, to the extent that the property to which the restraining order relates is the same as the property that is sold or otherwise disposed of to satisfy the pecuniary penalty order and pay the costs, charges, expenses and remuneration referred to in subsection 49 (6)\"; (d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (g) \"19 or\" after \"section\". (2) The amendments made by subsection (1) apply in relation to restraining orders made before or after the commencement of this section.  Crimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2) No. 123, 1991 Production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ebc54048cf2b016daf885a03b24131b32520795ec0b80f9f6c5628930eecace1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-49-ss-1 ;
